This extension adds Resident Evil 2 modding support to Vortex Mod Manager.
[summary]Fluffy and REFramework automatically installed.[/summary]

[color=#ffff00][size=4][b]If you used the Vortex extension prior to the 2.0.0 Fluffy migration, you MUST complete the following steps:[/b][/size][/color]
[list=1]
[*][b]Verify your game files in Steam (or other game store).[/b][/*]
[*][b]Reinstall ALL mods in Vortex. You can use Shift+Click to select multiple mods and Reinstall them all at once using the blue bar at the bottom.[/b][/*]
[*][b]Enable all mods in Fluffy Mod Manager to complete installation. You can launch Fluffy via the button on the deploy notification.[/b][/*]
[*][b]If you have not used Vortex for this game prior to 2.0.0, you can safely ignore and suppress the startup notification using the "Never Show Again" button.[/b][/*]
[/list]
Fluffy Mod Manager and REFramework will be automically installed.

[b]✅ Supported Versions:[/b]
[list]
[*]Steam[/*]
[*]Steam Demo[/*]
[*]Xbox[/*]
[*]Other versions may need to select the installation location manually.[/*]
[/list]
[b]🛠️ Mod Installation Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]Fluffy Mod Manager installs to the game folder, recognised by a "modmanager.exe" file.[/*]
[*]REFramework installs to the game folder, recognised by a "dinput8.dll" file.[/*]
[*]Loose Lua/Plugin (REFramework) mods with a ".lua" file outside the REFramework folders install to the "reframework\autorun" folder.[/*]
[*]Binaries / Root Folder mods with a "nvngx_dlss.dll" file or a ".exe" file install to the game folder.[/*]
[*]Fluffy Preset mods with a ".prt" file install to the "Games\RE2R\Presets" folder.[/*]
[*]Any other mod not described above installs to the "Games\RE2R\Mods" folder.[/*]
[*]Archives with a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with ModuleConfig.xml) are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead.[/*]
[/list]
[b]📋 Usage Notes:[/b]
[list]
[*]You can open several useful files/folders/URLs using the buttons within the folder icon on the Mods toolbar.[/*]
[*]Automatically installs[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/site/mods/818] Fluffy Mod Manager[/url] (FMM) and [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/residentevil22019/mods/1097][/url][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/residentevilrequiem/mods/13]REFramework[/url]﻿﻿﻿ (for plugins and script mods). You must run FMM to install mods into the game data archives.[/*]
[*]Installs mods with .exe files or a few select dlls directly to the game root folder (bypassing Fluffy).[/*]
[*]For mods not to be used with FMM (upscalers, reshades, etc.), you will need to change the mod type to "Binaries / Root Folder" and unzip the mod in the staging folder.[/*]
[/list]

[b]📝 Notes for Mod Authors:[/b]
[spoiler]
Packaging rules for Resident Evil 2 mods, so Vortex installs them to the right place.

Vortex decides what a mod is by looking at the files and folders inside the archive. It tries each installer in order and the first one that matches wins, so archive layout is what determines where your mod ends up.

========================================================================

Fluffy Mod Manager (tool):

This installer handles Fluffy Mod Manager, not mods for it. It exists so users can install Fluffy Mod Manager through Vortex, and mod authors normally never package this.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a file named "modmanager.exe" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - If you bundle Fluffy Mod Manager inside your mod archive, Vortex treats the whole download as Fluffy Mod Manager rather than as your mod. Ship the mod alone and list Fluffy Mod Manager as a requirement.

========================================================================

REFramework (mod loader):

This installer handles REFramework, not mods for it. It exists so users can install REFramework through Vortex, and mod authors normally never package this.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a file named "dinput8.dll" in the archive.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - If you bundle REFramework inside your mod archive, Vortex treats the whole download as REFramework rather than as your mod. Ship the mod alone and list REFramework as a requirement.

========================================================================

Loose Lua Scripts:

Standalone REFramework Lua scripts, shipped without the surrounding REFramework folder structure.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by a ".lua" file in an archive that does NOT already contain a REFramework folder ("reframework" or "autorun").
    - Vortex adds the correct folder structure around the script for you.

  Installs to: "reframework\autorun"

  Common mistakes:
    - Including an REFramework folder as well switches the archive to a different installer, which expects the full structure to already be correct.

========================================================================

Root / Game Folder Mods:

For mods laid out the same way the files appear inside the game folder. Vortex copies the matched folder and everything under it straight into the game.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file named "nvngx_dlss.dll", "dstoragecore.dll", "dstorage.dll", "amd_fidelityfx_dx12.dll", "amd_ags_x64.dll" or "libxess.dll".
    - Recognised by any file with the ".exe" extension.

  Installs to: the game folder

  Common mistakes:
    - Zipping the folder that CONTAINS the game folders, instead of the game folders themselves, adds an extra level and misplaces every file.

========================================================================

Preset Files:

Configuration presets for REFramework mods.

  Requirements:
    - Recognised by any file with the ".prt" extension.

  Installs to: "Games\RE2R\Presets"

========================================================================

Fluffy-Format Mods:

The catch-all for RE Engine mods packaged in the normal Fluffy Mod Manager layout. Most content mods for this game land here, which is the intended outcome.

  Requirements:
    - Any archive not claimed by an earlier installer is treated as a Fluffy-format mod.
    - An archive already zipped in the Fluffy layout is installed as it is, with no repacking.

  Installs to: "Games\RE2R\Mods"

  Common mistakes:
    - Because this is a catch-all, a badly laid-out archive still installs - it just may not work. Match the layout Fluffy Mod Manager expects.

========================================================================

Rules That Apply To Every Mod Type:

    - Archives that contain a FOMOD installer (a "fomod" folder with "ModuleConfig.xml") are handed to Vortex's built-in FOMOD installer instead, and none of the rules above apply.
    - Folder and file name matching is case-insensitive.
    - Extra wrapper folders around a recognised folder are generally fine; the installer searches at any depth.
[/spoiler]

